<rss xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:content="http://purl.org/rss/1.0/modules/content/" version="2.0"><channel><title>纽约时报 实时热点</title><link>https://rss.nytimes.com/services/xml/rss/nyt/HomePage.xml</link><description>纽约时报 自动中文翻译源</description><docs>http://www.rssboard.org/rss-specification</docs><generator>python-feedgen</generator><lastBuildDate>Fri, 27 Nov 2026 20:10:03 +0000</lastBuildDate><item><title>随着价格上涨，美国人正在做出权衡而不是削减开支</title><link>https://www.nytimes.com/2026/11/27/business/inflation-consumer-spending-trade-offs-holidays.html</link><description>在强劲的消费支出中，许多家庭决定将钱花在他们最看重的膳食、旅行和活动上。&lt;hr&gt;&lt;b&gt;报道出处：&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;• [纽约时报] &lt;a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/11/27/business/inflation-consumer-spending-trade-offs-holidays.html'&gt;随着价格上涨，美国人正在做出权衡而不是削减开支&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;small&gt;原文：As Prices Rise, Americans Are Making Trade-Offs Rather Than Cutting Back&lt;/small&gt;</description><guid isPermaLink="false">https://www.nytimes.com/2026/11/27/business/inflation-consumer-spending-trade-offs-holidays.html</guid><pubDate>Fri, 27 Nov 2026 10:02:41 +0000</pubDate></item><item><title>黑色星期五优惠和假日销售对有影响力的人来说是大笔收入</title><link>https://www.nytimes.com/2026/11/27/business/influencers-black-friday-deals-holiday-shopping.html</link><description>品牌的黑色星期五和网络星期一营销策略越来越多地依赖于支付高价让社交媒体影响者发布视频。&lt;hr&gt;&lt;b&gt;报道出处：&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;• [纽约时报] &lt;a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/11/27/business/influencers-black-friday-deals-holiday-shopping.html'&gt;黑色星期五优惠和假日销售对有影响力的人来说是大笔收入&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;small&gt;原文：Black Friday Deals and Holiday Sales Are Big Money for Influencers&lt;/small&gt;</description><guid isPermaLink="false">https://www.nytimes.com/2026/11/27/business/influencers-black-friday-deals-holiday-shopping.html</guid><pubDate>Fri, 27 Nov 2026 15:29:05 +0000</pubDate></item><item><title>在民主党与特朗普的较量中，输家可能是联邦承包商</title><link>https://www.nytimes.com/2026/11/27/us/politics/trump-congressional-investigations-contractors.html</link>